      "math_academy_id": "e-3971",
      "problem": "Express $2^4 = 16$ in logarithmic form.",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n$a = b^x$ is equivalent to $\\log_{b}{a} = x$\n\nIf we compare $2^4 = 16$ with $a = b^x,$ we get $a = 16,$ $b = 2,$ and $x = 4.$\n\nTherefore, the equation $2^4 = 16$ can be expressed as $\\log_{2}{16} = 4.$",
